I've just released a new bugfix release of e2fsprogs 0.5b, dated
11-Mar-95, which replaces 14-Feb-95 release.  I encourage anyone using
the original 0.5b release, or the even older 0.5a release, to upgrade to
this latest version.

This released may be obtained via ftp from tsx-11.mit.edu, in the
directory /pub/linux/packages/ext2fs.

This is a bugfix release, which means that no new features were added.
(New features will appear in the 0.5c release, which is currently under
development.)  The bugs which were fixed include:

libext2: 
	* Added error checking to the llseek() compat code to protect
		against overflow.  This only applies to 1.0 and early
		1.1 kernels, which don't support the llseek() system call.

libss:
	* Install the libss shared library in /lib, since it's needed by
		debugfs (which is installed in /sbin).

e2fsck:
	* The file type statistics counters weren't being reset when 
		e2fsck reran pass 1 (which it needs to do after
		correcting a few types of filesystem corruption).  This
		was a cosemtic bug only.

	* When bitmap blocks were being reallocated, a fencepost error
		caused them to be allocated in the wrong block group.

mke2fs:
	* Mke2fs now clears the first 512 bytes of the filesystem.  This
		protects the newly created filesystem from being
		accidentally misidentified as a MS-DOS FAT filesystem.

	* Fixed bug where mke2fs would erroneously determine the size of
		a partition when (a) the filesystem was greater than 2GB
		*AND* (b) the device does not support the BLKGETSIZE
		ioctl.

badblocks:
	* Increase the space allocated for printing the block numbers,
		so that the display doesn't get corrupted when running
		badblocks on a very large partition.  (Cosemtic bug only).

	* Removed spurious seek errors which were reported when checking
		a device larger than 2GB.

fsck:
	* The check to ignore filesystems with a pass number of zero was
		accidentally deleted during the 0.5b development
		process.  This check was restored.

							- Ted

