Hello,

This morning, I uploaded pmirror-1.1.tar.gz and pmirror-1.1.lsm.
These files supersede the mirror-1.1.tar.gz and mirror-1.1.lsm files
that I uploaded last week.

This archive contains two perl scripts that can be used for
"mirroring" software from other ftp sites via anonymous ftp.  Their
value is that they can do this even if your only network connection
is via modem to a UNIX shell account.

I have exchanged scripts with Lee McLoughlin
(L.McLoughlin@doc.ic.ac.uk), the author of the original "mirror"
script used by most ftp sites.  His script is more general purpose,
but mine is easier to understand and supports modem only access, thus
making it more accessible to Linux users.

Here's the LSM:

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Begin3
Title:          pmirror
Version:        1.1
Entered-date:   95-03-09
Description:    Perl scripts for maintaining an up to date copy of any
                archive directory structure available from a UNIX host
                via anonymous ftp.  Can be used over a modem with ZMODEM.
                This is not the same as Lee McLoughlin <lmjm@doc.ic.ac.uk>'s
                mirror-x.y.tar.gz package, which is more general purpose.
Keywords:       Mirror Archive
Author:         dsnyder@netcom.com (David C. Snyder)
Maintained-by:  dsnyder@netcom.com (David C. Snyder)
Primary-site:   tsx-11.mit.edu /pub/linux/BETA/pmirror
                9925 pmirror-1.1.tar.gz
Alternate-site: sunsite.unc.edu pub/Linux/Incoming
                9925 pmirror-1.1.tar.gz
Original-site:  ftp.netcom.com /pub/ds/dsnyder
                9925 pmirror-1.1.tar.gz
Platform:       
Copying-policy:
End
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- David
