For those who like to play Majiong, there is now a QKMJ available.
Similar to Okbridge, you log in to a server and play with people
online.

The program's message is coded in Chinese Big5, you can convert it
to GB though.

It is available in sunsite:/pub/Linux/Incoming/qkmj*
could be moved to somewhere later though I have no idea.
You are referred to ftp://pbbs.chpi.edu.tw/pub/qkmj for
more information and clients for other platforms.

------------------------------------------------------------

To run the client:
	qkmj server_IP port_number
eg:
	qkmj 141.212.82.32 7001


To run your own server, start daemon as
	mjgps <port_number> &

port number is default to 6666. Use mjrec to maintain the user
record file.




README file:

This is the Linux (Majiong) qkmj server source and binary for client.
(client source is not released by author Candle yet)

The original site is ftp://pbbs.chpi.edu.tw/pub/qkmj/mjgps.

I modified it to be fully ANSI compatible and corrected a few bugs.
Mainly adding the header file and Makefile.

Thanks to Candle for his great work. You are referred to 
pbbs.chpi.edu.tw for more information. Typically, you can
bug him for providing 13 piece support.


