********************************************************************************
                   SIS - Single Image  Stereogram  generator
********************************************************************************


     This is my first announcement of sis, a single image stereogram gener-
     ator.  The  current  version  is  0.5,  which  I just uploaded to sun-
     site.unc.edu.

     SIS are also called SIRDS (Single Image  Random  Dot  Stereograms)  or
     just RDS, but sis has also the ability to read in textures besides the
     boring random dot generation, to make the SIS look nicer.

     Sis is a command-line driven tool, that reads in tiff  or  tga  depth-
     maps  and  produces  a sis in tiff format as output. The sources and a
     binary are provided. To recompile it,  you  need  libgr  (1.3),  which
     comes  along  with slackware. Some example depth-maps and textures are
     provided, too. I hope you have fun with it!


