either SunOS 4.1.3 or Solaris 2.3. The last two are untested. They are
available on ftp.waldorf-gmbh.de in:

  ftp.waldorf-gmbh.de in /pub/linux/mips/crossdev/sparc-sun-solaris2.3/gcc-2.6.3.tar.gz
                         /pub/linux/mips/crossdev/sparc-sun-solaris2.3/binutils-2.5.2.tar.gz
                         /pub/linux/mips/crossdev/sparc-sun-sunos4.1.3/gcc-2.6.3.tar.gz
                         /pub/linux/mips/crossdev/sparc-sun-sunos4.1.3/binutils-2.5.2.tar.gz
                         /pub/linux/mips/crossdev/i486-unknown-linux/gcc-2.6.3.tar.gz
                         /pub/linux/mips/crossdev/i486-unknown-linux/binutils-2.5.2.tar.gz

If there are people out there that require binaries for another hostmachine
or that have built the tools for another machine, please mail me. I'm
especially interested in binaries for the MIPS based DEC machines.

Most people - especially foreigners - will prefer to use the mirror sites due to the
much higher bandwidth. Mirror sites include:

  ftp.uni-mainz.de (134.93.178.132) in /pub/Linux/arch/mips
  sunsite.unc.edu  (198.86.40.81)   in /pub/Linux/ALPHA/mips

List of changes (incomplete...):

  - Fix the binutils prototype problem with basename(3) and libc-4.6.27.
  - Fixed the %hi, %HI and %lo operators in gas for MIPS targets.
  - Due to the strong interest in Linux for R3000 based machines
    the compiler now defaults to R3000 code, no more R4600.
  - Added new relocation type required to build libc for MIPS.

  Ralf

